
PART 1: OFFICIAL ENGINEERING PROJECT SYNOPSIS

Project Title: SecurEdge-Vision: A Trusted Multi-Tier Edge Surveillance Platform with Dynamic Identity Whitelisting and Real-Time Threat Interdiction Engine
Domain: Artificial Intelligence, Computer Vision, Edge Computing

1. Introduction

Traditional Closed-Circuit Television (CCTV) systems function purely as passive recording systems. They rely heavily on human security personnel for continuous monitoring and post-incident investigation. This approach introduces operational delays, fatigue-driven oversight, and a complete lack of proactive intervention.
SecurEdge-Vision shifts the paradigm from passive recording to active, automated threat interdiction. Designed as a fully local edge application running on standard consumer laptop hardware, the platform integrates parallel deep learning models to identify known individuals, recognize strangers, and immediately detect severe threats like firearms, heavy weapons, or accidental fire hazards.

2. Problem Statement
Existing security surveillance frameworks face three critical bottlenecks:
1. High Latency & Cloud Dependency: Standard smart cameras stream footage to external cloud servers for AI inference. This results in heavy bandwidth consumption, vulnerability to network outages, and delayed response times during active emergencies.
2. Context-Blind Alert Systems: Current motion-detection cameras generate frequent false alarms from harmless movements because they cannot differentiate between an authorized individual (e.g., a family member or courier) and an actual intruder.
3. Absence of Weapon/Hazard Detection: Standard CCTV pipelines provide no real-time structural analysis of weapon presence or life-threatening environmental hazards (like fire), delaying emergency response until manual confirmation is achieved.

3. Objectives of the Project

• Zero-Cloud Edge Computing: To engineer a low-latency computer vision pipeline capable of processing high-definition local frame streams entirely on consumer-grade laptop hardware.
• Dual-Engine Inference Multiplexing: To construct a unified architecture executing simultaneous facial vector analysis and real-time deep learning object detection on a single input stream.• Dynamic Identity Triage: To segment incoming subjects instantly into a Dynamic Classification Array featuring four distinct operational tiers: Core Owner, Family Member, Courier Agent, and Threat/Thief.
• Graded Alert Automation: To deploy a responsive UI Escalation Matrix that maps threat severity levels directly to specific alert actions, bypassing default operational queues when a weapon is present.

4. Methodology & System Architecture

The system follows a strict five-tier data progression architecture executed locally:
1. Frame Ingestion: Real-time video inputs are captured via the local laptop webcam or an offline file stream using the OpenCV Input Buffer.
2. Offline Cloud Training: Custom-curated datasets for specialized threat vectors (pistols, heavy weapons, fire) and authorized user faces are annotated and trained on Google Colab to generate optimized weights without taxing the deployment hardware.
3. Multiplexed Edge Inference: The incoming array frame is fed concurrently to:1. 
	• YOLOv8 Module: Scans array segments for structural anomalies matching trained weapon or fire parameters.
	• 128-D Face Encoding Module: Maps facial geometry into a 128-Dimensional Euclidean vector matrix to check against a pre-loaded local whitelist database.
2. Triage Classification Matrix: The joint inference metadata is evaluated. An unknown face combined with a weapon detection instantly triggers the highest threat tier.
3. Streamlit UI Escalation Dashboard: Acts as the centralized local application layer, rendering real-time bounding boxes and updating the UI Alert Matrix state instantly.

